.\" Leon Boot Menuconfig — Man Page
.TH LBM 1 "2026-08-09" "lbm 0.7.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lbm \- Leon Boot Menuconfig: edit Leon's boot.toml in a menuconfig-style TUI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lbm
.RI [ config_path ]
.RI [ entries_file ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lbm
is the interactive, menuconfig-style editor for Leon's boot configuration
.br
.RI ( boot.toml ).
It is a pure-Rust TUI built with
.B cursive
(crossterm backend; no ncurses dependency) and is themed strictly black and
white with the classic menuconfig look: a highlighted selection row, bracketed
items, and
.RI ( value )
annotations.
.PP
The editor understands exactly the keys the bootloader reads: \fItimeout\fR
(integer seconds), \fIsplash\fR (whether the boot menu is shown),
\fIdefault_entry\fR (the label booted automatically), \fItheme\fR, and
\fIentries_file\fR. Unset keys are omitted on save, byte-for-byte matching what
\fBlbc config set\fR writes and what
.BR lbl (1)
validates on every boot. The on-disk file stays single-quoted-literal-friendly,
so backslash-heavy values like
.I \eEFI\eleon\eentries.jsonc
round-trip unchanged.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I config_path
The
.I boot.toml
to edit. Defaults to
.IR ~/.config/leon/boot.toml .
.TP
.I entries_file
The bootloader's auto-generated entries file
.RI ( entries.jsonc ,
defaulting to
.IR \eEFI\eleon\eentries.jsonc )
to feed the "Default Boot Entry" picker and the "Discovered Boot Entries"
view. When omitted, lbm probes the usual ESP mount points
.RI ( /boot/efi ,
.IR /boot ,
.IR /efi ).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B Save
Write the current configuration to the selected
.I boot.toml
(also available with Ctrl+S).
.TP
.B "Save & Exit"
Save and leave the editor.
.TP
.B Exit
Leave without saving (asks first when there are unsaved changes; Ctrl+Q quits).
.SH KEYMAP
.TP
.B Up / Down
Move the selection.
.TP
.B Enter
Select the highlighted item / toggle
.IR splash .
.TP
.B Esc
Back out of the current dialog or cancel an edit.
.TP
.B Ctrl+S
Save the configuration.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Q
Quit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/leon/boot.toml
The host copy of the boot configuration edited by
.BR lbm .
.TP
.I \eEFI\eleon\eboot.toml
The copy the bootloader actually reads; stage it with
.B "lbc stage"
or
.B "lbc config set"
to mirror changes onto an ESP.
.TP
.I \eEFI\eleon\eentries.jsonc
The auto-generated boot-entries file written by the bootloader on every boot,
used by lbm's entry picker.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lbl (1),
.BR lbt (1),
.BR lbc (1),
.BR leon-common (7)
